WEBVTT

00:03.300 --> 00:10.328
TakeSync lines up every camera, recorder and lav mic by their sound, and hands you a timeline that's ready to edit.

00:10.378 --> 00:12.112
Let me show you how it works.

00:13.213 --> 00:14.844
First, one simple rule:

00:14.894 --> 00:16.453
one device, one track.

00:16.503 --> 00:22.887
Add each camera and each recorder on its own, not one big folder with everything inside.

00:24.388 --> 00:29.792
Drag the first device's folder into the window, or click Source folder.

00:29.842 --> 00:34.325
Memory cards like AVCHD or P2 are recognized automatically.

00:35.425 --> 00:38.979
Each next device goes into the empty slot on the left.

00:39.029 --> 00:40.181
Forgot some files?

00:40.231 --> 00:42.250
Drop them on that track's name.

00:43.350 --> 00:47.109
If a folder has proxy files, TakeSync asks about them.

00:47.159 --> 00:51.412
Usually, click Skip proxies, so the sync uses your originals.

00:52.512 --> 00:54.927
The audio analysis starts on its own.

00:54.977 --> 01:00.987
You can keep adding sources while it runs, and a file analyzed once is never decoded again.

01:02.087 --> 01:04.527
When it's done, click Synchronize.

01:04.577 --> 01:06.577
Keep Correct audio drift on:

01:06.627 --> 01:10.237
it fixes recorders that run slightly fast or slow.

01:11.337 --> 01:14.129
Every clip now sits in the order it was shot.

01:14.179 --> 01:17.098
Yellow clips were placed by the camera's clock.

01:17.148 --> 01:18.866
Red ones couldn't be synced.

01:18.916 --> 01:22.150
Press Shift and the down arrow to jump between them.

01:23.250 --> 01:25.425
Press P to check the sync in the player.

01:26.525 --> 01:29.923
Now click Export timeline and choose your editor.

01:29.973 --> 01:32.526
For Premiere Pro you get an XML file.

01:32.576 --> 01:40.687
You can also export audio or video files, add a sequence with the recorder's sound, and mark or move unsynced clips.

01:41.787 --> 01:42.581
Click Export.

01:42.631 --> 01:47.125
Then click the file to show it in Finder, and import it into Premiere.

01:48.225 --> 01:54.938
Settings has the language, the waveform style, color skins, the analysis cache and your license.

01:56.037 --> 02:04.164
MP4, MOV, WAV and AIFF work out of the box on Apple Silicon.

02:04.214 --> 02:09.887
For MXF, MTS or MKV, click Install FFmpeg.

02:10.988 --> 02:12.078
And that's it:

02:12.128 --> 02:15.501
one device per track, Synchronize, Export.

02:15.551 --> 02:19.412
Try TakeSync free for seven days at takesync.uk.
